.SH NAME
frontend/node_modules/es-set-tostringtag Directory Reference
.SH SYNOPSIS
.br
.PP
.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.SH "es-set-tostringtag \*{[![Version Badge][npm-version-svg]][package-url]\*} "
.PP
\fR\fP \fR\fP [][license-url] \fR\fP

.PP
\fR\fP
.PP
A helper to optimistically set Symbol\&.toStringTag, when possible\&.
.SH "Example"
.PP
Most common usage: 
.PP
.nf
var assert = require('assert');
var setToStringTag = require('es\-set\-tostringtag');

var obj = {};

assert\&.equal(Object\&.prototype\&.toString\&.call(obj), '[object Object]');

setToStringTag(obj, 'tagged!');

assert\&.equal(Object\&.prototype\&.toString\&.call(obj), '[object tagged!]');

.fi
.PP
.SH "Options"
.PP
An optional options argument can be provided as the third argument\&. The available options are:
.SS "\fRforce\fP"
If the \fRforce\fP option is set to \fRtrue\fP, the toStringTag will be set even if it is already set\&.
.SS "\fRnonConfigurable\fP"
If the \fRnonConfigurable\fP option is set to \fRtrue\fP, the toStringTag will be defined as non-configurable when possible\&.
.SH "Tests"
.PP
Simply clone the repo, \fRnpm install\fP, and run \fRnpm test\fP 
